e United States to Mexico, Christmas changed a little bit. Now we have a big dinner with my family, my aunts [snorts] and cousins and grandparents. We eat turkey, potato salad, cheesy spaghetti, and warm bread. Then we drink bonche like a sweet fruit punch at night. But my favorite Christmas food is pie. Any kind of pie. Pumpkin pie, apple pie, cherry pie, cheesecake pie, any kind of pie. What's your favorite Christmas food? I also love The Day of the Dead, but I think Christmas wins. Christmas is the winner. What is your favorite holiday? Maybe I've never heard of it. So tell me why you celebrate that holiday, how you celebrate that holiday, and where? This was a little challenge for my absolute beginner listeners, but with my hand gestures and pictures, I hope you were able to understand it all. If you didn't, let me know what new word you learned today. See you next time. Bye. [music] >> [music] [music]",
